{
  "version": "cc_human_domain_rules_pilot_v2",
  "note": "Pilot rules v2, from the 2026-10-30 domain precision review (450 hand-labelled pilot documents, data/task-roots/cc-human/precision-v1). Pilot documents never enter cohorts, so these lists may be public; production rules are loaded from a private file (--rules) and stay private until the pool retires. Hosts match the host or any subdomain (an optional /path prefix narrows a host). Patterns are ASCII regexes, case-insensitive unless they start with (?-i). Tier 1 (hosts, host patterns, strong paths) decides first, in priority order. Then content cues: a domain needs min_cues distinct cues on the page and min_excerpt_cues of them (and an anchor, when it lists anchors) in the chosen excerpt; the most page cues win, ties by priority. Then tier 2 (weak hosts, weak host patterns, weak paths) fires only when its domain has weak_min_cues cues on the page and weak_min_excerpt_cues in the excerpt. Everything else is general_web.",
